                <pb facs="0671" n="583" xml:id="pg583"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Newberry.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-08-19"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Foster instructs Mr. Newberry to urgently make the following demands in the
                    ease of Dr. Bartlett, at Bourdour: First, for effective protection; second,
                    sufficient pecuniary indemnity; third, punishment of all the guilty; fourth,
                    reprimand of officials if proved remiss; and informs him that a vessel will be
                    sent to investigate if these demands fail.</p>
            </div>
